== (1) prefix fixed points are the 2-adic convergents of n ==
 x_(w_j) = n mod 2^(A_j): True; U^j(n) - n = D_j (x_(w_j) - n)/2^(A_j): True; product identity |n - x|_2 |n - x|_oo = |U^j n - n|_2 |U^j n - n|_oo / |D_j|: True
 n = 27: (j, clock > 0, x_(w_j), U^j(27)) for j <= 12: [(1, False, '-1', 41), (2, False, '-5', 31), (3, False, '-23/11', 47), (4, False, '-85/49', 71), (5, False, '-287/179', 107), (6, False, '-925/601', 161), (7, False, '-2903/1675', 121), (8, False, '-9221/4513', 91)]
 the positive-clock prefixes with x_(w_j) < 27 are the value-level descents; 27 descends at j = 37
== (2) THM-4512's threshold is the prefix fixed point; the precision residual ==
